{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/909242-magically-indced-breaking-points","id":909242,"title":"Magically Indced Breaking Points","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-07T10:00:03-07:00","id":909242,"title":"Magically Indced Breaking Points","content":"Okay I'm wondering how magically induced breaking points work on various splats.<br /> <br /> Vampires are obvious it would work like any other breaking point a vampire faces. Same with Mages.<br /> <br /> But from there I have no clue.<br /> <br /> I don't know how the intrigity stat works for Demons.<br /> <br /> Giest hasn't been updated for 2e.<br /> <br /> Werewolves, if say something say a Changeling contract causes a breaking point, is it a breaking point for spirit or a breaking point for flesh?<br /> <br /> Beasts don't normally have breaking points being the creepy fuckers they are (love Beasts), but could a Mage spell force a breaking point on them, with the possiblity of losing satiety?<br /> <br /> Using a magic to cause a breaking point in a Changeling can back fire with a lucky roll by the Changeling so it possible for them to lose or GAIN clarity from the breaking point.<br /> <br /> I don't know what the mortality stat is for Deviant.<br /> <br /> Hunters work like humans, because most of them are humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T10:35:33-07:00","id":909267,"title":"","content":"I think it depends entirely on the power in question. I can't think of any powers that just say &quot;Causes a breaking point.&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T10:36:55-07:00","id":909269,"title":"","content":"I'd say none of them suffer Breaking Points because Breaking Points are a feature of Integrity, and they don't have Integrity. Supernatural means of triggering a Breaking Point either need to explicitly spell out how they affect other Integrity Equivalents or they would have no effect. As I see it, anyways. Each Integrity Equivalent has so much internal baggage and variation, using a &quot;one size fits all&quot; model doesn't make sense anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T10:52:00-07:00","id":909282,"title":"","content":"Seconding Vent0; Integrity traits aren't interchangeable enough for this. Even Humanity and Wisdom might not necessarily always be appropriate risks of detachment or hubris where something would otherwise cause a breaking point through shock; Wisdom reflects behavior, while 2e Humanity reflects distance from the mortal human experience. Harmony works on a different model, while demons' Cover and beasts' Satiety are completely irrelevant to experiencing shock or guilt. Supernatural shocks just don't affect most supernatural beings in the same way they affect humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:28:59-07:00","id":909365,"title":"","content":"There's been hints that, in Changeling at least, there are antagonist powers that strip Clarity (and PC powers that risk it). IIRC, Demon Exploits risk Cover, Beasts can choose to spend Satiety, some Cruac reduces Humanity. However, almost all of these are self-inflicted, meaning they can't target another line's Integrity-equivalent, with the possible exception of Huntsmen and their Clarity-drain attacks. I would assume that only works on Clarity, and not other equivalents. <br /> <br /> Not sure if that answers the question posed. Of course, I'm not sure exactly what question <i>was</i> posed. Because &quot;witnessing magic causes Breaking Points&quot; only applies to Integrity, I think; none of the others have Breaking Points for that (&quot;doing magic&quot; maybe, but not witnessing it). Same with &quot;having magic generally done to you&quot;. And I don't know of any powers that cause Breaking Points directly (Mage's Mind might have it, because Mage has everything).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:45:34-07:00","id":909385,"title":"","content":"I could see a Mage with Spirit being able to shift Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T14:26:33-07:00","id":909481,"title":"","content":"Okay the l looked at Mage and Changeling playtest Doc, and the only power I found that I think reads as a universal breaking point, is Paralysising Shudder, a 5 dot contract.<br /> <br /> Apocolpyse the Prine 4 dot spell should be able to cause a breaking point in Changelings given the spells, description, not just mortal intigrity, but the spell makes it sound like its that breaking point is not universal, so I think it open to interruptation.<br /> <br /> I could see it causing a breaking point towards spirit if using spirit mage sight, or flesh is using matter or life mage sight in Werewolves.<br /> <br /> I'll check Beast next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:07:49-07:00","id":909658,"title":"","content":"Why on earth would Apocalypse trigger a Breaking Point for Changelings? Gaining Mage Sight has nothing to do with reminding them of their Duramce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:34:00-07:00","id":909680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/909242-magically-indced-breaking-points?p=909658#post909658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why on earth would Apocalypse trigger a Breaking Point for Changelings? Gaining Mage Sight has nothing to do with reminding them of their Duramce.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it likely would assault their understanding of the world around them, their ability to perceive what is true and what is not. Ironic, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:52:11-07:00","id":909699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/909242-magically-indced-breaking-points?p=909680#post909680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it likely would assault their understanding of the world around them, their ability to perceive what is true and what is not. Ironic, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but that's not what causes Clarity Breaking Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T20:38:17-07:00","id":909788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/909242-magically-indced-breaking-points?p=909699#post909699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but that's not what causes Clarity Breaking Points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither is reminding them of their Durance, lest we forget nearly every breaking point developed after character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T20:53:40-07:00","id":909798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/909242-magically-indced-breaking-points?p=909788#post909788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neither is reminding them of their Durance, lest we forget nearly every breaking point developed after character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's <i>one of the things</i> that causes Clarity Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A character\u2019s two starting triggers should follow the below criteria:<br /> <br /> \u2022 One trigger must tie directly to the changeling\u2019s manner of captivity. This could be reflected in the service she conducted in Faerie, it could be literally tied to a material or type of object, a specific behavior, or whatever reminder of why she had to leave.<br /> \u2022 Another trigger should reflect what she lost in her abduction. It\u2019s a place where she mentally detached when leaving the mortal world, and has yet to reconcile that loss. This could be a broad concept such as fidelity, a specific thing such as sexual contact, honesty, children, repetitive work, a place, or any other thing that made her captivity strike hard.<br /> <br /> Additional triggers do not have to follow these rules. Instead, they should reflect the changeling\u2019s existence since the escape, and any specific trauma he\u2019s experienced. </div> </div> </div>Gaining Mage Sight could <i>maybe</i> be the foundation of a new Trigger, but it's not going to immediately cause a Breaking Point against Clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T09:08:19-07:00","id":910122,"title":"","content":"It makes me think of what would happen if the Changeling decided to Keen while they had Active Mage Sight up.<br /> <br /> Also a Clarity 10 Changeling has +5 to perception rolls as well as rolls invovling riddles and figuring things out.<br /> <br /> +5 to any rolls using the Mage Sight basically.<br /> <br /> So maybeca high clarity Changeling is nearly as capable of using active Mage Sight as a Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}